{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Or on a distant road.</b> Pointed over the heh — to interpret that רחוקה does not attach to דרך, since the dot is over the heh, which is as if it is not there. Rather, it attaches to איש — that is, if he is far away." "<b>Or for your generations.</b> That is: <b>or on a distant road for you</b> — now; <b>or</b>, when this matter happens to you, for your generations."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:08.652738771Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}